        <body>
            <div xml:id="d371">

                <pb facs="0485" n="377" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg377"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Foster to Mr.
                            Durham.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-02-09"><hi rendition="#italic">February 9,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Foster informs Mr. Durham that, while diplomatic settlement may be hoped for,
                    the President does not wish to use naval force to enforce reparation. He
                    instructs him to continue a firm course diplomatically and to suggest that
                    negotiations should not be embarrassed by the question of amount, which if
                    reasonable, would be acceptable.</p>


                <xi:include href="d371-a1.xml" xpointer="d371-a1"/>
